Problem Statement : Given an integer array, find the subarray with the largest sum and return the sum of the elements present in that subarray.

Brute Force Approach: 
Main idea: Find all possible subarrays, calculate the sum of each one, and store the largest sum in maxi.
- i — starting index of the subarray.
- j — ending index of the subarray.
- k — traverses the selected subarray and adds its elements.
- sum — sum of the current subarray.
- maxi — maximum sum found so far.

Code:
for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
{
    for (j = i; j < n; j++)
    {
        sum = 0;

        for (k = i; k <= j; k++)
            sum += arr[k];

        maxi = max(sum, maxi);
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n^3)
Space Complexity: (O(1)

Better Solution:
Instead of recalculating the sum of each subarray from scratch, we maintain a running sum.
1. Select a starting index i.
2. Initialize sum = 0.
3. Move the ending index j from i to the last element.
4. Add nums[j] to the running sum.
5. Update maxi whenever a larger sum is found.
6. Repeat for every starting index.

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    int maxSubArray(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        int maxi = INT_MIN;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int sum = 0;

            for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {
                sum += nums[j];
                maxi = max(maxi, sum);
            }
        }

        return maxi;
    }
};
Time Complexity: (O(n^2)
Space Complexity: (O(1)

Optimal Solution: Kadane's Algorithm
if the running sum becomes negative, discard it before considering the next element. A negative running sum only reduces the sum of a future subarray.

For every element:
1. Add the current element to sum.
2. Update maxi with the largest sum found so far.
3. If sum becomes negative, reset it to zero.
4. Continue to the next element.
We initialize maxi to INT_MIN so that arrays containing only negative numbers are handled correctly.

Code:
class Solution {
public:
    int maxSubArray(vector<int>& nums) {
        int sum = 0;
        int maxi = INT_MIN;

        int Start = 0;
        int ansStart = 0;
        int ansEnd = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            if (sum == 0) {
                Start = i;
            }

            sum += nums[i];

            if (sum > maxi) {
                maxi = sum;
                ansStart = Start;
                ansEnd = i;
            }

            if (sum < 0) {
                sum = 0;
            }
        }

        return maxi;
    }
};
Time Complexity: (O(n)
Space Complexity: (O(1)
